-- title:
--   Tate point of the Γ₀(M')-rigidified problem and level automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$, and a non-zero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subset L((\mathsf q))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\ell$, $M'$ are units, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficient extension to $L$ of the $\mathsf q$-expansion `jq`, assumed non-zero. Assume: stability of the Katz level-$\ell$ predicate `IsLevelPStructure` and of the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt` under variable changes (`hℓ`, `hM`); group laws $\mathcal G$ over $A$ that are chord–tangent and have the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ at $q$ that is a section transport; and the existence, for every $A$-algebra and every variable change resp. coefficient homomorphism, of graded homomorphisms of the projective-model graded rings realising it and satisfying the irrelevant-ideal condition (`hVC`, `hCO`). Let $\mathcal D$ be the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, whose level data consist of a tuple of polynomials $h_p$ indexed by the prime factors $p\mid M'$ with `IsGamma0PowAt` at $(p,v_p(M'))$, a Katz level-$\ell$ datum, and a Drinfeld pair at $q$. Finally let $\rho\colon\Gamma_0(M')\to\mathcal D.\mathrm{ProblemAut}$ satisfy: for every $\gamma$, every field $T$ over $A$ and raw data $x,x'$ over $T$ with the discriminant of the Drinfeld curve of $x$ a unit, if $x'$ has the same curve, the same $\Gamma_0$-tuple, Katz datum relabelled by the integral matrix of $\gamma$ and Drinfeld pair relabelled by the same matrix, then $(\rho\gamma)$ carries the class of $x$ to the class of $x'$. Then there exists a point $x_0$ of $\mathcal D$ over $K$ such that: (a) $j(x_0)$, read in $L((\mathsf q))$, equals `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`, the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{q\ell}$ in the $j$-series; (b) there are a variable change $C$ over $L((\mathsf q))$ and a raw datum $r$ over $K$ with class $x_0$, such that, writing $(X_1,Y_1)$ for the cusp point `cuspPoint L (q*ℓ) ξ ![1,0]`, one has $C.u\,(2X_1+1/6)=2Y_1+X_1$, $C.r=-1/12$, $C.s=-1/2$, $C.t=1/24$; the curve of $r$ pushed to $L((\mathsf q))$ equals $C\bullet$ `tateBase L (q*ℓ)`; for each prime $p\mid M'$, each field $F'$ with a homomorphism $f\colon L\to F'$ and each primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta\in F'$, the $p$-component of the $\Gamma_0$-tuple of $r$, pushed to $F'((\mathsf q))$, is the transport by $C$ (via `kernelVariableChangeDeg` in degree `gamma0PowDeg`) of $\prod_{1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p\nmid a}(X-x(\text{toric point at }\zeta^a))$; the Katz level-$\ell$ datum of $r$ pushed to $L((\mathsf q))$ is the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData L (q*ℓ) ξ` at $(q,0)$ and $(0,-q)$; and there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData L (q*ℓ) ξ` at $(\ell,0)$ and $(0,-\ell)$, through which the sections $P$ and $Q$ of the Drinfeld pair of $r$ pass in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`; and (c) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ that is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt` for the data $L,\ q\ell,\ \xi,\ q\ell,\ (q\ell)^2M',\ H$ (so that on quotients of $\mathsf q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_H$ the effect of $\tau$, read through $\iota$, is the slash action of `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`), the functoriality of $\mathcal D$ along $\tau$ sends $x_0$ to $(\rho\gamma)$ applied to $x_0$.
--
--   This is the Tate-point identification step for the $\Gamma_0(M')$-rigidified full-level Weierstrass moduli problem: it produces a single $K$-point sitting at the Tate curve with prescribed level data at $\ell$, at $q$ and at each prime power dividing $M'$, and shows that the level automorphisms of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ act on this point exactly through the pinned automorphism $\rho(\gamma)$. It is used in the fibre-dictionary and automorphism-count arguments for the rigidified problem, and in the corresponding statement with the $A$-algebra structures supplied separately.
